WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.720
- Every once in a while at the show,

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:03.910
we like to head outside to
meet up with our friends

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:08.013
for a socially distant chat
we call a Drive-Interview.

00:00:08.013 --> 00:00:09.862
(audience cheers)

00:00:09.862 --> 00:00:12.695
♪ Drive Interview ♪

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:15.150
(Kelly sings)

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.710
That's my favorite one.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.270
Recently I caught up with NASCAR superstar

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:22.440
Kurt Busch, which isn't easy
to do 'cause he's really fast,

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.479
do you get it? 'Cause
NASCAR. I know you get it.

00:00:24.479 --> 00:00:27.152
Check it out!
(audience laughs)

00:00:27.152 --> 00:00:29.735
(guitar music)

00:00:34.848 --> 00:00:37.265
(rock music)

00:00:42.073 --> 00:00:45.239
(car engine revs)

00:00:45.239 --> 00:00:46.081
(tires screech)

00:00:46.081 --> 00:00:47.831
All right, all right!

00:00:49.017 --> 00:00:50.946
Okay, that's rad.
(both chuckle)

00:00:50.946 --> 00:00:54.180
You just rolled up here
looking like that. Okay.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.013
Wow.

00:00:55.013 --> 00:00:55.846
- [Kurt] Hi Kelly!

00:00:55.846 --> 00:00:58.660
- This was the raddest! You win, you win-

00:00:58.660 --> 00:00:59.730
Is this the real deal?

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:00.900
- I had to make an entrance.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:05.040
Yes, this is an old race car.
When we have the race cars,

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.860
they turn into show cars
afterwards, we don't quite put

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.060
them out in the pastures.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:11.150
- That's seriously so badass.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:11.983
- Thank you.

00:01:11.983 --> 00:01:13.543
- This is the coolest one yet.

00:01:17.394 --> 00:01:19.360
Have, have cars always been your thing?

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.000
- My dad had race cars in the
garage and then street rods.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.160
- Wow.
- And so,

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.110
every time we went to the track,

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:28.610
like as a kid, it was a way of life.

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:29.443
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- [Mark] And so whether

00:01:29.443 --> 00:01:31.100
it was Friday or Saturday night,

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.310
it was to go see Dad race,
and so that's how I grew up.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:37.030
- Wow. Was there, I don't
know, any pressure since your

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.096
Dad was such a car guy and into
that? Was there any pressure

00:01:39.096 --> 00:01:41.440
the first time behind the wheel with him?

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:44.970
- There was, I, I felt like
when we went to the track,

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.870
he was there to win.
He didn't make friends,

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:49.960
he was just there to win. And
so, when I was growing up,

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:53.390
like it was a perfectionist
feel with cars.

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:56.820
And so I'm like fifteen and a
half, got my learners permit,

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.850
and he's teaching me how
to drive and he's like,

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:01.180
all right, pull into the bank right now.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.060
I pull in and things start
hucky-puckying around

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.380
and I stall it.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:07.940
And I was devastated 'cause
I just wanted to be perfect

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.410
for my Dad, especially with cars.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.340
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:14.890
I heard that your wife is a
polo player, which first of all,

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:16.660
I don't know that I've
ever met a polo player.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:20.011
So like that's pretty cool
but do you ride horses?

00:02:20.011 --> 00:02:22.480
- I'm not so good on the horses.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:23.890
But, I can come back strong.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:26.700
She's not so good on the go-carts.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.980
But I love to support her polo and

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.750
the feel of the team
camaraderie and the competition,

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.490
it's very, very equal to the racing world.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:38.210
With competition, your
horses, the saddles, the cars,

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:39.043
the equipment.

00:02:39.043 --> 00:02:41.420
- Yeah, I love the
sound of horses running.

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:42.266
- [Mark] Yes.

00:02:42.266 --> 00:02:43.410
- [Kelly] Like I think its the
coolest sound in the world.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:48.127
I, and I, man, like your
children have to competitive.

00:02:48.127 --> 00:02:49.065
(both chuckle)
- [Mark] Oh yeah.

00:02:49.065 --> 00:02:50.930
- [Kelly] Like there's no
way they're not going to be

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:51.763
with Mom and Dad.

00:02:51.763 --> 00:02:52.840
- They can choose what they want to do

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:54.370
but it's going to end up being that way.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:55.620
- [Kelly] That's amazing.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:01.030
I have been to so many NASCAR
events, and I will tell you

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.090
I feel like a lot of the NASCAR think,

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:05.770
obviously the driving is
the epicenter of it all,

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:09.250
but it's like a country
music festival to me.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.870
It's like people come for
the music but they also come

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:15.780
for like the get together. It's
like a giant family kind of

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:17.810
environment. Everybody's
into it, drinking,

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:19.820
having a good time. Like,
are you excited about the

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:21.910
new season, that people are
actually going to be there?

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.190
- Yeah last year with COVID and the break

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:25.750
that we went through,

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.410
all the new protocols were
put in place to create

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:32.190
the bubble. And to protect
the teams, the drivers, and-

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.023
- Which is important.

00:03:33.023 --> 00:03:35.750
- Yes, and the officials,
everybody, and the fans.

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:38.250
And now with things starting
to trickle back into place,

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:41.170
we're getting that feel
of our fans coming back,

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:45.000
I mean the first race back,
it was like the twilight zone.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.410
We didn't have the
tailgating, we didn't have the

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:50.270
camaraderie and the
partying going on before,

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:53.670
leading up into the race. And
then after the race it was

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:56.673
eerie. Like the guy won,
he's in victory lane and-

00:03:57.621 --> 00:03:59.060
we're all like what is going on?

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:01.343
So we miss the soul of our fans.

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:05.530
- Thank you so much. I'm
such a fan, you're like

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.760
even cooler in person. And
I'm so excited for y'all

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.730
to get back to this season and
have like fans in the stands

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:14.230
and it becoming more of a norm again.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:16.720
- Thank you. No, this environment,
right now, just sitting

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.340
in our cars and enjoying a conversation.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:20.740
That's what people do at the tracks.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:22.330
And our fans are coming back,

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:24.570
the states are opening
up a little bit. But,

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.640
of course we all have to
be safe and we'll have our

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.550
full capacity yet to come.

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:30.470
- Yeah. Absolutely. Well, small steps.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.420
- Tune in all right? If you
can't be there in person,

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:33.253
you gotta tune in.

00:04:33.253 --> 00:04:35.040
- Yeah. I will tune in.
- All right, here we go.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.140
We'll see you on the flip side.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:38.210
- All right, later!

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.437
- You got it.
- Bye!

00:04:39.437 --> 00:04:44.437
- Bye!
(woman chuckles)

00:04:46.993 --> 00:04:49.890
(audience claps)

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:52.110
- Well I love Kurt Busch.
So I got a new friend,

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:54.260
I love him so much and hey
Kurt please tell your wife

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.610
Ashley thank you so much for the gift.

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:57.340
She makes these really
bathing suits y'all.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:00.230
Monarch Reign. They are
so cute. And I love it.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:02.770
And I look really good in
it. So thank you Ashley.

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:04.710
But y'all can keep up
with Kurt Busch on the

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:06.780
NASCAR cup series all season long.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:08.853
Check your local listings for race times.

